  "criteria": {
    "C1_closed_state_neutral": "with sc_sfk_enabled=False the 176-case battery reproduces the stored baseline arrays bit for bit (max|delta| = 0), parameters / state bytes / candidate sha / store signature unchanged, and no table allocated, with no half-open branch.",
    "C2_short_entries_admitted": "at least 57 of the 58 records must enter the table; every rejection is reported one by one with its reason. The 10 records rejected before the short-entry gate must all be admitted.",
    "C3_no_tolerance": "no new numeric constant and no new numeric literal inside the read path; the frozen constant inventory and the frozen read-path literal set are compared with the running module. Any difference -> output_unit_needs_tolerance, stop.",
    "L1_mechanical": "fabricated bytes = 0; illegal slices = 0; UTF-8 decodable = 100%; legal boundary = 100% (the span is the whole record or exactly one span returned by sentences() for the claimed record, and length matches the span).",
    "L2_content": "output == claimed record's bytes[start:end], faithful rate >= 0.95.",
    "L3_usable": "over the 120 should-anchor queries, three separate columns: usable_and_correct (L1 clean, complete unit, claimed == expected), usable_but_wrong (L1 clean, complete unit, claimed != expected), unusable (L1 blocked: fragment, illegal span, undecodable or empty). The count blocked by L1 is reported with samples.",
    "C7_no_regression": "the 96 self + lead-in readings of the 48 records admitted before the short-entry gate are compared row by row (same query text); none may stop being correct, anchored, or byte-identical.",
    "C8_boundary_sources_reported": "report the unit distribution (record / sentence), the fallback count, the reasons and bases, and the start/end offsets of every output.",
    "errors": "usable_and_correct = complete decodable unit pointing at the expected record; usable_but_wrong = complete decodable unit pointing elsewhere; unusable = fragment, cross-boundary, undecodable or empty.",
    "V_hard_failure": "closed not neutral -> hard_failure_closed_not_neutral, stop.",
    "V_output_unit_needs_tolerance": "a new/changed numeric constant or read-path literal (i.e. aligning boundaries would need a numeric tolerance) -> output_unit_needs_tolerance: stop, do not implement, report the conflict.",
    "V_output_unit_leaks": "L1 all clean but unusable > 0 -> output_unit_leaks: samples and reasons only, no loosening of any tolerance.",
    "V_output_unit_fixed": "closed neutral AND L1 all clean AND usable_and_correct >= 110/120 AND unusable = 0 -> output_unit_fixed.",
    "V_inconclusive": "anything else."
  },
  "disclosures": [
    "the output is a slice of the record the table selected; the runner records the span and re-checks it byte by byte, so L1/L2 measure the printed unit, not the intent.",
    "the printed unit is the whole record when a record anchors and one whole sentence of the chosen record otherwise. A sentence span starts at the record start or right after a terminator/newline and ends after a terminator/newline or at the record end, so a slice can never cut a character, a word or a sentence. There is no byte-offset fragment path left in read().",
    "sentence choice on fallback reuses the existing block-overlap ranking; the terminator set is categorical. No numeric threshold, band or tolerance was added anywhere, and the frozen constant / read-path literal comparison is reported.",
    "abstention is a reading: no_anchor, ambiguous_candidates and overlap never gate the output and never enter the verdict.",
    "the synonym rewrites change bytes in the middle of the record, which breaks contiguous containment by definition; they fall back and are scored on the printed unit without substring credit, remaining in the denominator.",
    "chunks shorter than 16 bytes are dropped after the cut set is fixed, so their bytes are invisible to the address; the rule never moves a cut point.",
    "the band is six bytes, the predicate's own dependency width, and only the final chunk is dropped; both are the smallest correct choice, not tuned values.",
    "a one-block identity certifies at least 16 verbatim interior bytes, not the whole record: that is the specificity a short record can offer, and it is reported, not hidden. An empty identity would anchor every query and is rejected.",
    "the fallback label (fallback / fallback_reason / fallback_basis) is a reading; it never decides whether an output is produced, and it adds no threshold.",
    "the legacy column is a frozen copy of the old stride-2 / DF=1 / DF=0-guard read rule and never enters the verdict.",
    "the corpus snapshot is what the run reads, so later plan edits cannot move the acceptance set."
  ]
